{
 "title": "IBIS-AMI 106G PAM4 optical link",
 "group": "Photonic links",
 "description": "53.125 GBd PAM4: IBIS-AMI Tx (FFE + driver BW) -> MZM -> 2 km O-band -> PD/TIA -> IBIS-AMI Rx DSP (11-tap FFE + DFE + MM CDR)",
 "schematic": {
  "notes": [
   {
    "x": 40,
    "y": -140,
    "title": "IBIS-AMI 106G PAM4 optical link \u2014 what this testbench does",
    "lines": [
     "TX1 is an IBIS-AMI transmitter (pf_tx) sending 53.125 GBd PAM4",
     "(PRBS-15, Gray-coded) with a 3-tap FFE and a 35 GHz driver bandwidth,",
     "into MZM1 biased at quadrature. 2 km of O-band fiber, PD1 and a",
     "32 GHz TIA1 follow: the 100G-per-lane DR optics.",
     "RX1 is an IBIS-AMI receiver in DSP mode: 11-tap FFE (3 pre-cursors,",
     "MMSE in Init, LMS in GetWave), 1-tap DFE, Mueller-Muller CDR, PAM4",
     "slicers on adapted levels, 1.5 mV rms input noise.",
     "",
     "The MZM's sine transfer compresses the outer PAM4 levels: the Link",
     "tab's 'linear fit' residual and the gap between the statistical BER",
     "(with and without that distortion) show what IBIS-AMI's LTI view",
     "misses. Raise TX1 v1/v0 to +/-1.0 V and rerun."
    ]
   }
  ],
